<section class="ai-notice">
  <div class="ai-notice-container">
    <div class="ai-notice-icon">🤖</div>
    <div class="ai-notice-content">
      <h3>An AI Experiment</h3>
      <p>Zena is implemented almost entirely by generative AI—an experiment to see what happens when you ask AI to build a new programming language. This is a real project with real goals, but also a test of whether AI can create well-constructed, reliable software with human oversight. The hope is that AI can make it drastically cheaper to build not just the language, but the entire ecosystem needed to launch it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>Why Zena?</h2>
    <p>Built from the ground up for WebAssembly with modern language features.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="features-grid">
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon perf">⚡</div>
      <h3>High Performance</h3>
      <p>Zero-cost generics via monomorphization. Classes map directly to WASM GC structs with no runtime overhead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon types">🔷</div>
      <h3>Sound Type System</h3>
      <p>Strong static typing with no implicit coercion. If it compiles, it won't have type errors at runtime.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon wasm">🎯</div>
      <h3>WASM-GC Native</h3>
      <p>Designed specifically for WebAssembly GC. Produces small, efficient binaries optimized for the web.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon familiar">📝</div>
      <h3>Familiar Syntax</h3>
      <p>TypeScript-like syntax that feels natural. Arrow functions, classes, generics—all the features you love.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon safe">🛡️</div>
      <h3>Safe by Default</h3>
      <p>Immutable bindings and data structures by default. Nominal typing prevents accidental structural compatibility.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon modern">✨</div>
      <h3>Modern Features</h3>
      <p>Generics, inheritance, auto-accessors, and more. Inspired by TypeScript, Dart, Kotlin, and Swift.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section code-section">
  <div class="code-container">
    <div class="code-description">
      <h2>Write code that feels familiar</h2>
      <p>Zena's syntax is designed to be intuitive for developers coming from TypeScript, JavaScript, or other C-family languages.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clean class syntax with constructors</li>
        <li>Arrow functions everywhere</li>
        <li>Generic classes and functions</li>
        <li>Explicit type annotations where needed</li>
        <li>Exports for host interop</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-dot red"></span>
        <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
        <span class="code-dot green"></span>
        <span class="code-filename">Point.zena</span>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="comment">// A simple class representing a 2D point</span>
<span class="keyword">class</span> <span class="type">Point</span> {
  <span class="punctuation">x:</span> <span class="type">i32</span>;
  <span class="punctuation">y:</span> <span class="type">i32</span>;

  <span class="comment">// Constructor</span>
  <span class="function">new</span>(<span class="punctuation">x:</span> <span class="type">i32</span>, <span class="punctuation">y:</span> <span class="type">i32</span>) {
    <span class="keyword">this</span>.x = x;
    <span class="keyword">this</span>.y = y;
  }

  <span class="comment">// Method</span>
  <span class="function">distanceSquared</span>()<span class="punctuation">:</span> <span class="type">i32</span> {
    <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="keyword">this</span>.x * <span class="keyword">this</span>.x + <span class="keyword">this</span>.y * <span class="keyword">this</span>.y;
  }
}

<span class="keyword">export</span> <span class="keyword">let</span> <span class="function">main</span> = ()<span class="punctuation">:</span> <span class="type">i32</span> <span class="operator">=></span> {
  <span class="keyword">let</span> p = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="type">Point</span>(<span class="number">3</span>, <span class="number">4</span>);
  <span class="keyword">return</span> p.<span class="function">distanceSquared</span>(); <span class="comment">// Returns 25</span>
};</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section feature-status-section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>Roadmap & Status</h2>
    <p>Zena is in active development with a robust core and a clear vision for what's next.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-status-grid">
    <div class="feature-status-card">
      <h3>What's Already Here</h3>
      <ul class="feature-checklist">
        <li class="checked"><strong>WASM-GC Native:</strong> Generics are monomorphized (no boxing), and classes map directly to WASM structures.</li>
        <li class="checked"><strong>Sound Type System:</strong> Static types with no implicit coercions. No runtime type errors for safe compiles.</li>
        <li class="checked"><strong>Modern Syntax:</strong> Exhaustive pattern matching, records & tuples, sealed classes, mixins, and pipelines.</li>
        <li class="checked"><strong>Optimizations:</strong> Compilation-driven dead code elimination (DCE) producing compact WASM binaries.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-status-card">
      <h3>Current Focus & Next Steps</h3>
      <ul class="feature-checklist">
        <li class="unchecked"><strong>Self-Hosted Compiler:</strong> Complete the new IR-based backend, compile self-hosted, and retire the bootstrap compiler (Current Focus).</li>
        <li class="unchecked"><strong>Async Functions & WASM P3:</strong> Native async/await support with cooperative multithreading.</li>
        <li class="unchecked"><strong>WASI Component Model & WIT:</strong> Import `.wit` files and target WASI components directly.</li>
        <li class="unchecked"><strong>Tooling & DX:</strong> A package manager, online playground, and enhanced VS Code integration.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

